+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry validates tool calls against the schema declared for the tool before the executor handles model input.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- `execute` validates input against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema`; rejected input returns a `ToolResponse` describing the failure and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input that violates the schema before invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L11)).
+- Valid input, including properties absent from the schema, reaches the executor unchanged and exactly once ([validated by: rejects input that violates the schema before invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L11)).
+- A function-valued tool definition is resolved for each call, and each call is checked against the schema returned for that call ([validated by: validates each call against its current function-valued tool schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L39)).
+- An uncompilable static schema makes `register` throw synchronously with an error naming the tool ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable static schema at registration](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L60)).
